      "intel_summary": "All three source IPs are classified as malicious. 198.51.100.23 and 198.51.100.77 belong to the 198.51.100.0/24 range, a known host-scanning and brute-force source network. 203.0.113.141 falls in the 203.0.113.0/24 range associated with a distributed credential-stuffing botnet. No IPs were rated suspicious or unknown.",
      "enrichment_notes": "The threat intel significantly escalates concern. Three factors align: (1) the incident already shows hallmarks of an automated credential-stuffing/brute-force campaign \u2014 90 login attempts in ~7 seconds from 3 IPs targeting 18 usernames including SQLi and XSS payloads, all failing with 401s; (2) every source IP is confirmed malicious infrastructure (two from a dedicated scanner/brute-force range, one from a known credential-stuffing botnet); (3) the botnet link implies coordinated, distributed attack capacity that can easily rotate or scale.\n\nThe zero successful logins is the only mitigating signal \u2014 the attack has not yet breached accounts \u2014 but the combination of velocity, payload diversity, and verified malicious infrastructure means this is an active, high-confidence intrusion attempt that warrants immediate blocking, alerting, and credential-stuffing defence review (rate limits, MFA enforcement, account lockout policies).",
